cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Modeling the Water–Energy–Food Nexus in a Brazilian Periurban Watershed: An Agent-Based Simulation Under Climate Change Scenarios"
abstract: >
  Agent-based model (ABM) simulating Water-Energy-Food (WEF) nexus dynamics in
  the Alto Tietê basin (UGRHI 6, São Paulo, Brazil) across a historical baseline
  and two IPCC AR6 climate scenarios (SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5), under contrasting
  water-governance regimes (fragmented vs. integrated). Integrates open datasets
  from ANA, ANEEL, MapBiomas (Collection 10.1), and IPCC AR6. Developed for a
  manuscript submitted to Water (MDPI), Special Issue "The Water-Energy-Food
  Nexus: Toward Integrated Solutions for Sustainability".
